1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,480
Senna, what's this about?

2
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,360
Kobito's Happy Birthday party!

3
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:19,060
I'm heading into town on Sunday to shop for presents.

4
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,440
Do you think you can make it?

5
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,520
This coming Sunday?

6
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,140
Yeah, I think I'm free.

7
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:27,940
Sounds good.

8
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:30,540
Let's meet up around 1 o'clock at the train station.

9
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:31,520
See you there.

10
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,660
You get me.

11
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:36,180
Oh!

12
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,320
You ready for some fun?

13
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:41,260
Tie Rika to a telephone pole and she'll take whatever you give her.

14
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:44,260
Rika likes to be on top, but she can't resist a forceful man,

15
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,840
the kind that goes in on the first date.

16
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,900
Please call back. Rika's ready and waiting.

17
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:50,760
Leave me alone.

18
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,980
Read it vertically.

19
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:54,580
Vertically, huh?

20
00:00:54,580 --> 00:01:00,580
Rika wants you to take her on a date, please.

21
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:02,640
No can do.

22
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:03,580
Pretty please?

23
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,040
Rika needs your help in picking a present for Kobito.

24
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,120
Then why didn't you tell me that the first time?

25
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:10,040
You get me.

26
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:13,360
For the esteemed Mr. Kodaka Hasegawa.

27
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,080
Dear Mr. Kodaka Hasegawa,

28
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:20,020
I hope this pleasant fall season has brought you great wealth and prosperity,

29
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,380
particularly in the forging of new friendships.

30
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,280
Please forgive me for the suddenness of this letter.

31
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,340
I know its arrival is unexpected.

32
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:30,940
I'm terribly sorry to trouble you when you are surely very busy,

33
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:35,860
but I take pin in hand now because there is something of utmost importance that I must ask you.

34
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:38,540
There is no other companion I may consult.

35
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,540
I know you are a busy man,

36
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:43,760
so I shall be so bold as to come straight to the point.

37
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,660
Your sister's birthday is fast approaching.

38
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:49,260
What should I give to your honored sibling?

39
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,060
With my best wishes for your health and...

40
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:53,520
I don't have time for a novel.

41
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:54,220
You get me.

42
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,740
Need your help getting a present for Kobito.

43
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,800
No big deal if you're busy or whatever.

44
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,040
I know how forgetful I'm like you are, but whatever.

45
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,860
Tomorrow would work best, but whatever.

46
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:04,800
It's not like you absolutely have to be there,

47
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,580
so don't worry if you're like busy or whatever.

48
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:06,920
And it's super long.

49
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:09,140
It's not like I can't pick out one little present of my own or whatever.

50
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:09,900
What's with all the whatevers?

51
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,420
Anyway, I guess I'll see you there.

52
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:13,560
Oh well.

53
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:23,440
Hey, what's up?

54
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,080
The next train is now approaching platform 3.

55
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,180
Looks like everyone's here.

56
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:27,880
Cool.

57
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:29,820
Guess we better get to it.

58
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:30,740
Complete stops.

59
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:08,324
Grab a seat, Yozara. There's one right here.

60
00:04:08,564 --> 00:04:10,044
Shut up. Don't tell me what to do.

61
00:04:10,404 --> 00:04:11,884
What's the rest of the club doing here?

62
00:04:12,604 --> 00:04:13,684
Oh, my bad.

63
00:04:14,144 --> 00:04:15,544
Yeah, I guess I didn't tell you.

64
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:18,004
Everyone wanted to buy Kobito a present,

65
00:04:18,184 --> 00:04:20,484
so I figured we might as well hit up the mall together.

66
00:04:20,824 --> 00:04:24,104
Still, this probably wasn't the best way for you to go about it.

67
00:04:24,364 --> 00:04:26,244
I mean, it's not a secret that you're pretty dense,

68
00:04:26,324 --> 00:04:27,824
but this is beyond stupidity.

69
00:04:27,944 --> 00:04:29,264
Did I do something wrong?

70
00:04:29,364 --> 00:04:30,664
Never mind, idiot.

71
00:04:30,664 --> 00:04:33,844
Rika had a feeling Kodika was going to let her down again,

72
00:04:34,124 --> 00:04:36,864
but even though you know it's coming, it still sucks.

73
00:04:36,924 --> 00:04:39,244
I, too, feel your pain. I think we all do.

74
00:04:39,884 --> 00:04:42,864
All her studies couldn't have prepared Rika for such a man.

75
00:04:43,384 --> 00:04:46,824
Someone so, so ridiculously oblivious to everything.

76
00:04:47,364 --> 00:04:47,804
Okay.

77
00:04:48,144 --> 00:04:49,624
Oh, but it's really not a big deal.

78
00:04:49,864 --> 00:04:52,564
One day you'll feel Rika's presence emotionally and physically.

79
00:04:52,724 --> 00:04:53,644
I don't think I will.

80
00:04:53,844 --> 00:04:56,464
By the way, why are you wearing your lab coat today?

81
00:04:56,864 --> 00:04:58,304
Why? Is there a problem with it?

82
00:04:58,304 --> 00:05:00,124
You've been obsessed with your hair lately,

83
00:05:00,244 --> 00:05:01,644
but you don't care about your clothes.

84
00:05:01,804 --> 00:05:03,444
It's kind of a strange combination.

85
00:05:04,124 --> 00:05:06,104
Like today, how you're wearing the same clothes,

86
00:05:06,184 --> 00:05:07,824
but also randomly got highlights.

87
00:05:08,204 --> 00:05:10,244
Um, Rika didn't think you would notice.

88
00:05:11,004 --> 00:05:12,544
Aren't you just full of surprises?

89
00:05:13,004 --> 00:05:14,904
But to be honest, Rika has never thought

90
00:05:14,904 --> 00:05:16,844
that worrying about her clothes would make a difference.

91
00:05:16,844 --> 00:05:20,284
There's no incentive considering you don't even pay attention to her

92
00:05:20,284 --> 00:05:21,204
when she's stripping.

93
00:05:21,604 --> 00:05:22,544
Not gonna lie.

94
00:05:22,624 --> 00:05:24,284
I wouldn't mind if she ditched the lab coat

95
00:05:24,284 --> 00:05:25,724
and wore something more revealing.

96
00:05:28,564 --> 00:05:32,004
I take it I somehow said all of that out loud again?

97
00:05:32,064 --> 00:05:32,584
Yeah, you did.

98
00:05:32,644 --> 00:05:33,964
Let's go in the back and make babies.

99
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:35,064
Oh, yeah.

100
00:05:35,204 --> 00:05:36,464
I've got a question, Senna.

101
00:05:36,804 --> 00:05:37,364
What is it?

102
00:05:37,944 --> 00:05:40,084
Rika wanted to buy some new clothes while we're shopping.

103
00:05:40,704 --> 00:05:42,384
Are there any nice stores you'd recommend?

104
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:45,384
You want my shopping advice, really?

105
00:05:45,944 --> 00:05:47,564
Rika would love to learn from the master.

106
00:05:47,744 --> 00:05:49,684
You're such a stylish and sexy gal.

107
00:05:50,064 --> 00:05:53,024
Actually, I honestly don't go shopping that often,

108
00:05:53,124 --> 00:05:55,844
and when I do, it's at the fancy name brand places near my house,

109
00:05:55,904 --> 00:05:57,084
so I don't know what to tell you.

110
00:05:57,804 --> 00:06:01,384
The only places close to your house are a few mountains and rice fields.

111
00:06:02,524 --> 00:06:03,724
Is that true, Senna?

112
00:06:04,064 --> 00:06:05,524
No, Miss Senna is fibbing.

113
00:06:07,284 --> 00:06:09,304
You're right. I'm sorry I lied to you.

114
00:06:09,924 --> 00:06:11,904
Stella's the one who picks out all of my clothes.

115
00:06:11,904 --> 00:06:14,384
She styles my hair and puts on my makeup, too.

116
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:15,664
What was that for?

117
00:06:15,844 --> 00:06:17,224
It's not like you know any better.

118
00:06:17,404 --> 00:06:18,984
Femininity level of only five.

119
00:06:19,364 --> 00:06:20,044
How pitiful.

120
00:06:20,324 --> 00:06:21,464
Hey, neat, a scouter.

121
00:06:21,784 --> 00:06:23,784
While we're at it, where do you buy your clothes, Yozara?

122
00:06:24,204 --> 00:06:25,684
I get all my stuff online.

123
00:06:25,984 --> 00:06:28,964
If I see a model with a decent-looking outfit in a fashion magazine

124
00:06:28,964 --> 00:06:30,864
or on a website, I'll buy the whole thing.

125
00:06:30,944 --> 00:06:31,684
Rika's jealous.

126
00:06:31,824 --> 00:06:35,104
It's awesome that you can look good wearing outfits straight out of a fashion bag.

127
00:06:35,364 --> 00:06:37,164
And today you look especially cute.

128
00:06:37,704 --> 00:06:38,664
This is cute?

129
00:06:38,664 --> 00:06:39,864
Shut up.

130
00:06:40,084 --> 00:06:40,484
Uh-uh.

131
00:06:40,664 --> 00:06:43,504
It's very feminine and such an adorable sort of sexy.

132
00:06:44,204 --> 00:06:44,684
Feminine?

133
00:06:45,644 --> 00:06:46,084
Adorable?

134
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:47,384
Sexy?

135
00:06:52,024 --> 00:06:53,424
Ah, crap.

136
00:06:53,604 --> 00:06:54,384
Take it back!

137
00:06:54,544 --> 00:06:56,244
This was in the how to look boyish section.

138
00:06:56,344 --> 00:06:57,724
There's no way this can be sexy.

139
00:06:58,184 --> 00:06:59,504
Girl, are you for real?

140
00:06:59,964 --> 00:07:01,764
Yozara, listen to me.

141
00:07:01,764 --> 00:07:05,724
When women rock the boyish look, it doesn't mean they're dressing like a man would.

142
00:07:05,804 --> 00:07:07,504
In fact, it's usually the other way around.

143
00:07:07,924 --> 00:07:11,084
It's a way to draw out your feminine charms by being more androgynous.

144
00:07:11,304 --> 00:07:14,004
Think shorts instead of skirts and knits instead of wolf-ins.

145
00:07:14,544 --> 00:07:15,024
Seriously?

146
00:07:15,384 --> 00:07:17,584
You'd have to be blind not to notice this stuff.

147
00:07:17,904 --> 00:07:22,104
How often do you see dudes strutting around in hot pants and showing off their belly buttons?

148
00:07:22,804 --> 00:07:26,564
But you're the only guy whose wardrobe I ever even noticed.

149
00:07:27,144 --> 00:07:27,444
Huh?

150
00:07:27,964 --> 00:07:29,284
Oh, just forget it!

151
00:07:36,864 --> 00:07:39,524
I'm gonna do some other shopping after I get her gift.

152
00:07:39,864 --> 00:07:41,104
Kodaka, you can't come along.

153
00:07:41,304 --> 00:07:41,844
That's cool.

154
00:07:42,224 --> 00:07:43,584
Are you gonna be okay by yourself?

155
00:07:43,924 --> 00:07:45,064
Rika will keep her company.

156
00:07:45,644 --> 00:07:45,864
Hmm.

157
00:07:46,364 --> 00:07:47,264
Yeah, all right.

158
00:07:48,744 --> 00:07:52,544
Yukimura, do you mind tagging along with Yozara and Rika and keeping them in line?

159
00:07:52,724 --> 00:07:55,304
We wouldn't want them to freak out in the middle of a public place.

160
00:07:55,364 --> 00:07:56,044
Do you know what I mean?

161
00:07:56,084 --> 00:07:56,464
Yes, sir.

162
00:07:56,464 --> 00:07:57,864
I've got it under control.

163
00:07:58,204 --> 00:07:58,924
I'll see you later.

164
00:07:59,244 --> 00:08:00,644
Best of luck shopping for Kobito.

165
00:08:01,084 --> 00:08:01,524
Thanks.

166
00:08:01,824 --> 00:08:02,504
Yeah, you too.

167
00:08:04,544 --> 00:08:07,384
Well then, that's that.

168
00:08:07,964 --> 00:08:09,684
Why don't the two of us start looking around?

169
00:08:09,684 --> 00:08:21,184
Hey, Kodaka, what's something I could buy for Kobito that'd make her like me more?

170
00:08:21,644 --> 00:08:23,664
I know she's into Full Metal Necromancer.

171
00:08:24,344 --> 00:08:27,564
Yeah, but she's pretty much got all the merchandise she could want already.

172
00:08:28,304 --> 00:08:31,984
Oh, and please, don't get her any expensive stuff.

173
00:08:32,364 --> 00:08:32,744
Hmm.

174
00:08:32,744 --> 00:08:35,884
You're a more considerate big brother than I thought.

175
00:08:36,524 --> 00:08:38,044
What would you recommend, then?

176
00:08:38,264 --> 00:08:39,504
I'm almost out of ideas.

177
00:08:40,284 --> 00:08:41,624
How about something you'd like?

178
00:08:41,784 --> 00:08:43,424
I totally want Kobito!

179
00:08:43,724 --> 00:08:44,764
You can't have her.

180
00:08:46,204 --> 00:08:47,384
Hey, over here.

181
00:08:47,384 --> 00:08:49,964
I just thought of a gift I know for sure she'd like.

182
00:08:50,104 --> 00:08:50,764
What's that?

183
00:08:51,124 --> 00:08:51,524
Meat.

184
00:08:52,004 --> 00:08:54,584
I mean meat the food, not meat as in you.

185
00:08:54,764 --> 00:08:56,024
Aw, I knew that.

186
00:08:56,104 --> 00:08:56,864
Don't rub it in.

187
00:08:57,184 --> 00:08:59,004
Steak, bacon, wings, anything.

188
00:08:59,404 --> 00:09:01,364
Get her some jerky and she's yours for life.

189
00:09:01,724 --> 00:09:05,624
Maybe so, but a meat snack's kind of a messed up birthday present, don't you think?

190
00:09:05,624 --> 00:09:07,264
Good point.

191
00:09:07,644 --> 00:09:08,064
Jerky?

192
00:09:08,244 --> 00:09:09,024
What am I thinking?

193
00:09:09,604 --> 00:09:09,924
Meh.

194
00:09:10,144 --> 00:09:12,324
Remember that as a last resort for the time being.

195
00:09:12,644 --> 00:09:14,124
I'm sure we'll find other good stuff.

196
00:09:14,284 --> 00:09:15,564
Oh my gosh, they have it!

197
00:09:15,904 --> 00:09:16,724
They have what?

198
00:09:16,984 --> 00:09:18,964
It's so beautiful.

199
00:09:19,644 --> 00:09:19,824
Hmm?

200
00:09:21,104 --> 00:09:25,164
Seriously, since when is the girl supposed to keep the guy company when they go shopping?

201
00:09:25,744 --> 00:09:27,084
Normally it's the other way around.

202
00:09:27,284 --> 00:09:27,724
Sorry.

203
00:09:28,424 --> 00:09:30,744
What the heck's so special about frying pans anyway?

204
00:09:31,204 --> 00:09:32,344
You've got to be kidding me.

205
00:09:32,744 --> 00:09:34,904
Default pans aren't just any old frying pans.

206
00:09:34,904 --> 00:09:37,244
Here, let me try and break it down for you.

207
00:09:37,244 --> 00:09:38,204
Not necessary.

208
00:09:41,364 --> 00:09:43,284
You are the weirdest person I know.

209
00:09:43,664 --> 00:09:45,104
It's almost kind of really sad.

210
00:09:45,204 --> 00:09:47,704
There's nothing wrong with liking high quality cookware.

211
00:09:47,864 --> 00:09:50,684
You've got a lot more issues than just that one, dummy.

212
00:09:51,084 --> 00:09:51,724
Shut up.

213
00:09:52,244 --> 00:09:54,044
What do you think is taking the girls so long?

214
00:09:54,124 --> 00:09:56,324
Girls always take a long time to finish shopping.

215
00:09:57,144 --> 00:09:58,944
At least they're doing gaming games.

216
00:09:59,044 --> 00:10:00,604
You learned that from a video game?

217
00:10:00,604 --> 00:10:06,284
Hey, Kodika, what do you think of the other girls in the neighbor's club?

218
00:10:06,544 --> 00:10:07,644
Like, do you like them?

219
00:10:08,184 --> 00:10:09,204
What do you mean?

220
00:10:11,304 --> 00:10:13,024
Man, why are you so...

221
00:10:13,024 --> 00:10:14,184
Ugh, never mind.

222
00:10:14,184 --> 00:10:18,724
Do you ever even think about dating and having a girlfriend?

223
00:10:19,364 --> 00:10:22,284
I guess I wouldn't say I don't not want to date.

224
00:10:22,584 --> 00:10:24,204
Thanks for clearing that up.

225
00:10:24,524 --> 00:10:27,164
Well, for right now, my main goal is to make some friends.

226
00:10:27,824 --> 00:10:28,624
Think about it.

227
00:10:28,644 --> 00:10:31,824
A boring guy without any friends isn't going to impress many ladies.

228
00:10:32,084 --> 00:10:33,584
Girls will think of him as a loser.

229
00:10:33,844 --> 00:10:36,204
I don't think that's necessarily true.

230
00:10:36,484 --> 00:10:36,584
Hmm?

231
00:10:36,584 --> 00:10:40,084
Oh, man, how are you so...

232
00:10:40,084 --> 00:10:42,224
Ugh, never mind.

233
00:10:42,304 --> 00:10:43,884
Hey, why do you keep saying that?

234
00:10:45,804 --> 00:10:47,104
A random question.

235
00:10:48,104 --> 00:10:52,944
Um, well, what do you think about the fact that Yozara and I used to be friends?

236
00:10:53,424 --> 00:10:54,884
You know, when we were kids.

237
00:10:55,064 --> 00:10:55,324
Hmm.

238
00:10:56,364 --> 00:11:00,044
I was honestly surprised when you first told us, but then I thought things over.

239
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:01,784
I don't think it's that big a deal.

240
00:11:01,864 --> 00:11:03,364
In fact, it doesn't matter at all.

241
00:11:03,584 --> 00:11:05,424
You mean you don't care?

242
00:11:05,424 --> 00:11:07,264
Well, I mean, it's in the past, right?

243
00:11:07,524 --> 00:11:09,444
The present is what's really important.

244
00:11:10,284 --> 00:11:11,664
Yeah, I guess you're right.

245
00:11:12,844 --> 00:11:16,604
Still, I haven't quite figured out what Yozara's intentions are with you.

246
00:11:16,864 --> 00:11:17,424
With what?

247
00:11:17,704 --> 00:11:18,524
Never mind.

248
00:11:19,164 --> 00:11:21,084
I doubt I'm going to lose to her anyway.

249
00:11:21,524 --> 00:11:22,204
That's all.

250
00:11:24,984 --> 00:11:26,464
Hey, before I forget.

251
00:11:26,884 --> 00:11:30,044
And this is important, so please make sure you remember it.

252
00:11:32,344 --> 00:11:34,084
Don't think of yourself as boring.

253
00:11:34,084 --> 00:11:36,744
Anybody I like can't be that lame.

254
00:11:40,864 --> 00:11:43,504
Do you have any opinions on Rika's new outfit?

255
00:11:43,904 --> 00:11:46,804
This is what the clerk recommended Rika try on for you.

256
00:11:47,004 --> 00:11:47,284
Oh?

257
00:11:47,684 --> 00:11:48,084
Well, it's...

258
00:11:48,704 --> 00:11:51,664
I'd say that whenever you try to look good, you pull it off nicely.

259
00:11:52,024 --> 00:11:54,684
Rika will interpret that messed up comment as a compliment.

260
00:11:55,944 --> 00:11:57,104
Um, Kodaka?

261
00:11:57,704 --> 00:11:58,864
Do you think I look okay?

262
00:11:59,264 --> 00:12:01,844
Yozara bought something else, so she let me have this.

263
00:12:01,844 --> 00:12:03,604
Damn, Yukimura, that's hot.

264
00:12:04,184 --> 00:12:06,724
Uh, I mean, it looks nice on you.

265
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:08,704
I'm very glad you like it.

266
00:12:08,944 --> 00:12:09,524
Thank you.

267
00:12:09,844 --> 00:12:11,264
Last but not least...

268
00:12:11,264 --> 00:12:12,684
What the hell is that?

269
00:12:12,684 --> 00:12:15,404
What are you wearing?

270
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:16,824
I'm so confused, woman.

271
00:12:16,904 --> 00:12:18,404
You're a disaster in black cotton.

272
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,864
Oh, be quiet, flapjacks.

273
00:12:20,064 --> 00:12:22,104
I'm not in the greatest of moods right now.

274
00:12:22,184 --> 00:12:23,144
A tracksuit?

275
00:12:23,484 --> 00:12:25,604
I found it marked down at a sports store.

276
00:12:25,864 --> 00:12:26,884
Don't you like it?

277
00:12:27,444 --> 00:12:30,364
Anyway, all these crowds are making me kind of groggy.

278
00:12:30,704 --> 00:12:33,084
I'll just grab something for Kobudo near my place.

279
00:12:33,184 --> 00:12:33,784
See you later.

280
00:12:33,984 --> 00:12:34,204
Huh?

281
00:12:34,204 --> 00:12:36,104
Rika's gonna head home, too.

282
00:12:36,304 --> 00:12:37,184
Thanks for the fun.

283
00:12:38,124 --> 00:12:39,024
Sorry, Senna.

284
00:12:39,184 --> 00:12:41,864
My bags are getting heavy, and I'm tired of lugging them around.

285
00:12:42,004 --> 00:12:42,924
Not you, too!

286
00:12:43,084 --> 00:12:44,464
I shall accompany you, Kodaka.

287
00:12:44,684 --> 00:12:46,344
You have got to be kidding me!

288
00:12:46,464 --> 00:12:48,924
You guys are so the worst shoppers ever!

289
00:12:48,924 --> 00:12:59,524
There, it's perfect, but no surprise there.

290
00:13:00,524 --> 00:13:05,004
Then again, do you think Kobudo will even enjoy having a birthday party that looks this lame?

291
00:13:05,264 --> 00:13:06,204
Cut us some slack.

292
00:13:06,304 --> 00:13:09,164
No one here actually knows what a normal birthday party looks like.

293
00:13:09,344 --> 00:13:10,484
This'll have to work for now.

294
00:13:10,764 --> 00:13:14,324
Along those same lines, what are people supposed to do at a birthday party?

295
00:13:14,524 --> 00:13:15,344
Do you know, Kodaka?

296
00:13:15,344 --> 00:13:20,344
Uh, well, probably eat cake and open presents most of the time, though that doesn't sound

297
00:13:20,344 --> 00:13:21,304
like a lot of fun.

298
00:13:21,524 --> 00:13:22,944
Maybe everyone plays games.

299
00:13:23,044 --> 00:13:24,144
It's a party, after all.

300
00:13:24,384 --> 00:13:25,864
Fat chance that's gonna happen.

301
00:13:26,064 --> 00:13:29,444
The only games we have are your wonky computer games and Meets' pervy dates.

302
00:13:29,444 --> 00:13:30,224
Oh, please.

303
00:13:30,424 --> 00:13:32,044
There's no way she's not coming.

304
00:13:32,284 --> 00:13:34,104
Rika almost has all the bugs figured out.

305
00:13:34,504 --> 00:13:36,724
Yeah, too bad there aren't any board games in here, though.

306
00:13:36,984 --> 00:13:39,544
We'll just stop by the closest toy store and get one.

307
00:13:39,624 --> 00:13:40,664
How about Twister?

308
00:13:40,924 --> 00:13:42,104
You really are a pervert.

309
00:13:42,104 --> 00:13:47,344
If you're right outside the door, then you should just get in here.

310
00:13:51,724 --> 00:13:54,124
Happy birthday, my sweet darling Kobito!

311
00:13:56,864 --> 00:13:57,344
Likewise.

312
00:13:57,704 --> 00:13:59,184
Happy birthday, Miss Kobito.

313
00:14:00,024 --> 00:14:00,544
Poppers!

314
00:14:02,384 --> 00:14:03,964
Enough with the poppers, guys.

315
00:14:04,284 --> 00:14:05,924
Okay, Kobito, take a seat.

316
00:14:06,024 --> 00:14:07,164
It's time for your cake.

317
00:14:07,544 --> 00:14:09,824
Three, two, one, kick off!

318
00:14:09,824 --> 00:14:10,664
Dig in!

319
00:14:11,204 --> 00:14:11,564
Uh-huh.

320
00:14:11,704 --> 00:14:12,544
What do you think?

321
00:14:12,824 --> 00:14:13,904
Isn't it beautiful?

322
00:14:14,104 --> 00:14:15,224
We're so happy!

323
00:14:15,384 --> 00:14:16,324
Wow, Meat.

324
00:14:16,744 --> 00:14:19,224
Your creepiness never ceases to amaze me.

325
00:14:19,384 --> 00:14:20,244
What's your problem?

326
00:14:20,344 --> 00:14:22,104
That cake is incredible and you know it!

327
00:14:22,104 --> 00:14:32,464
It's a nice day for a birthmas.

328
00:14:33,064 --> 00:14:36,024
Happy birthmas for you.

329
00:14:36,704 --> 00:14:38,904
Who was born today?

330
00:14:39,324 --> 00:14:40,384
It was...

331
00:14:40,384 --> 00:14:41,324
Karla's birthday!

332
00:14:41,584 --> 00:14:43,504
Come on, at least get her name in sync.

333
00:14:45,664 --> 00:14:48,184
Happy birthmas to you.

334
00:14:48,184 --> 00:14:50,544
I hate that.

335
00:14:50,604 --> 00:14:51,784
Well, what are you waiting for?

336
00:14:51,944 --> 00:14:52,704
Blow out your candles.

337
00:14:52,844 --> 00:14:53,004
Oh.

338
00:14:53,764 --> 00:14:54,984
Um, okay then.

339
00:15:00,284 --> 00:15:01,604
Happy birth, Cheech!

340
00:15:01,744 --> 00:15:02,364
There you go.

341
00:15:05,124 --> 00:15:06,824
What'd you do that for, Hobag?

342
00:15:07,024 --> 00:15:08,424
Whoops, my finger slipped.

343
00:15:08,464 --> 00:15:09,744
Open white, Kodaka!

344
00:15:09,744 --> 00:15:17,044
They're each a different scent.

345
00:15:18,484 --> 00:15:19,884
It's a talisman.

346
00:15:26,424 --> 00:15:27,924
So you got her meat.

347
00:15:28,324 --> 00:15:29,024
Raw meat.

348
00:15:29,224 --> 00:15:30,144
Don't mock me.

349
00:15:30,484 --> 00:15:31,864
You're bound to eat some too.

350
00:15:32,384 --> 00:15:33,604
Meat giving meat.

351
00:15:33,944 --> 00:15:34,724
How original.

352
00:15:35,204 --> 00:15:36,364
I've got a good idea.

353
00:15:36,744 --> 00:15:38,044
Let's have sukiyaki tonight.

354
00:15:38,764 --> 00:15:40,124
Pretend that I'm right there

355
00:15:40,124 --> 00:15:41,784
spoon-feeding you my meat of love.

356
00:15:41,824 --> 00:15:42,164
No!

357
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:45,944
Sukiyaki!

358
00:15:48,024 --> 00:15:49,244
Someone's in a good mood.

359
00:15:49,804 --> 00:15:50,664
Ki-ki-ki.

360
00:15:51,004 --> 00:15:52,604
Today's been an awesome day.

361
00:15:55,184 --> 00:15:57,284
Hey, I've got to pick up some ingredients.

362
00:15:57,804 --> 00:15:59,184
Meet you back home in a little bit, okay?

363
00:15:59,384 --> 00:16:01,884
Do your best not to dawdle, my kinfolk.

364
00:16:04,724 --> 00:16:05,804
Oh, wow.

365
00:16:07,524 --> 00:16:07,964
Yo.

366
00:16:08,924 --> 00:16:10,084
I didn't see you.

367
00:16:10,284 --> 00:16:11,104
Why are you here?

368
00:16:11,264 --> 00:16:12,684
Um, that's my house.

369
00:16:12,984 --> 00:16:14,184
Why are you sneaking around?

370
00:16:14,764 --> 00:16:16,844
Oh, I was just hoping I could catch a glimpse

371
00:16:16,844 --> 00:16:17,944
of how it looks inside.

372
00:16:18,324 --> 00:16:18,964
That's all.

373
00:16:19,284 --> 00:16:19,784
Silly, isn't it?

374
00:16:19,784 --> 00:16:20,564
Yes, it is.

375
00:16:20,664 --> 00:16:22,464
Why do you even care how my place looks?

376
00:16:23,964 --> 00:16:25,644
Big Brother's finally home!

377
00:16:25,864 --> 00:16:27,644
And another unexpected visit.

378
00:16:28,064 --> 00:16:29,764
Did you get Kate to bring you over here?

379
00:16:30,024 --> 00:16:30,304
Yup.

380
00:16:30,664 --> 00:16:32,624
If there's anything the old hag is good for,

381
00:16:32,704 --> 00:16:33,764
it's taking me to see you.

382
00:16:33,764 --> 00:16:35,824
What are you still doing here?

383
00:16:36,024 --> 00:16:36,644
Stinking brat.

384
00:16:36,724 --> 00:16:37,944
Weren't you just begging and pleading?

385
00:16:38,064 --> 00:16:38,984
Please take me, sis.

386
00:16:39,024 --> 00:16:40,044
I'll be grateful forever.

387
00:16:40,284 --> 00:16:41,524
So what was that just now?

388
00:16:41,604 --> 00:16:42,684
Care to explain yourself?

389
00:16:42,864 --> 00:16:44,324
Um, I was...

390
00:16:44,324 --> 00:16:45,744
Get lost, poopy old hag!

391
00:16:47,524 --> 00:16:49,424
Honestly, something's wrong with that girl.

392
00:16:49,944 --> 00:16:52,124
Says the creepy chick who's been spying.

393
00:16:53,164 --> 00:16:54,764
Hey, since you two are here already,

394
00:16:54,844 --> 00:16:56,064
do you want to stay over for dinner?

395
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:57,164
Seriously?

396
00:16:57,364 --> 00:16:57,964
Both of us?

397
00:16:58,264 --> 00:16:58,964
Uh, yeah.

398
00:16:58,964 --> 00:17:02,304
Just perfect.

399
00:17:02,684 --> 00:17:05,504
This wonderful day has now turned into complete crap.

400
00:17:05,924 --> 00:17:09,244
So you must be Big Brother's one and only real little sister, huh?

401
00:17:09,524 --> 00:17:10,784
Who is your big brother?

402
00:17:11,224 --> 00:17:12,824
Oh, that's what Maria calls Kodika.

403
00:17:12,984 --> 00:17:14,504
She always wanted a bigger brother.

404
00:17:14,984 --> 00:17:17,524
So if I'm her sister and he's also older than me,

405
00:17:17,644 --> 00:17:18,944
then he's my big brother too,

406
00:17:19,024 --> 00:17:21,004
which totally makes you and I sisters.

407
00:17:21,004 --> 00:17:23,584
What's wrong?

408
00:17:23,984 --> 00:17:25,124
Crappy stupid head!

409
00:17:25,364 --> 00:17:26,304
You big fat dummy!

410
00:17:26,444 --> 00:17:28,364
How come you have so many little sisters now?

411
00:17:28,424 --> 00:17:29,964
I'm supposed to be the only sister.

412
00:17:30,064 --> 00:17:30,984
Quit making more!

413
00:17:31,064 --> 00:17:32,124
Whoa, calm down.

414
00:17:32,204 --> 00:17:33,404
They just call me Big Brother.

415
00:17:33,504 --> 00:17:34,544
It doesn't mean anything.

416
00:17:35,944 --> 00:17:38,524
Hey, why did Maria want to come over today?

417
00:17:39,084 --> 00:17:40,924
She said she wanted to talk to Kobito.

418
00:17:40,924 --> 00:17:42,284
Coo-coo-coo.

419
00:17:42,544 --> 00:17:45,424
What business does that foolish minion of God have with me,

420
00:17:45,544 --> 00:17:47,484
supreme ruler of darkness and destruction?

421
00:17:47,844 --> 00:17:49,664
Uh, what just happened?

422
00:17:49,664 --> 00:17:51,644
Just pretend you didn't see that.

423
00:17:53,104 --> 00:17:54,284
Hey, come on, Maria.

424
00:17:54,664 --> 00:17:57,164
Hurry up and give Kobito the present you bought for her.

425
00:17:57,944 --> 00:17:59,224
Maria brought a gift?

426
00:17:59,504 --> 00:17:59,784
Ah!

427
00:18:00,124 --> 00:18:02,364
Why'd you have to open your big mouth, poopy old head?

428
00:18:02,384 --> 00:18:03,884
Why are you freaking out about it?

429
00:18:05,824 --> 00:18:06,304
Here.

430
00:18:06,724 --> 00:18:08,884
I decided to be nice and get you a present,

431
00:18:08,884 --> 00:18:09,984
so you better like it.

432
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,344
Birthdays are kind of important,

433
00:18:12,504 --> 00:18:14,224
even for a poopy vampire like you.

434
00:18:14,304 --> 00:18:16,024
Just open it up and say thanks already.

435
00:18:19,664 --> 00:18:24,924
It's for scaring off evil spirits and spooky stuff.

436
00:18:25,124 --> 00:18:26,804
You should use it to drive out the darkness

437
00:18:26,804 --> 00:18:28,904
from your poopy soul and become a good girl.

438
00:18:29,124 --> 00:18:29,284
Hmm.

439
00:18:29,704 --> 00:18:31,564
What a silly little birthday present.

440
00:18:31,824 --> 00:18:33,744
Divine powers don't work on me.

441
00:18:34,064 --> 00:18:35,024
How dare you?

442
00:18:35,264 --> 00:18:37,724
Repent your dumb sins, you evil poopy vampire.

443
00:18:37,724 --> 00:18:39,624
Your stupid key has no effect.

444
00:18:39,624 --> 00:18:40,544
That's too, poopy vampire.

445
00:18:41,544 --> 00:18:44,004
All right, ladies, it's sukiyaki time.

446
00:18:44,044 --> 00:18:45,064
Ah, sukiyaki?

447
00:18:45,284 --> 00:18:47,264
That's that tasty-sounding meaty dish

448
00:18:47,264 --> 00:18:49,164
that the dumb hag's too stupid to make.

449
00:18:49,344 --> 00:18:49,664
Whee!

450
00:18:50,124 --> 00:18:51,204
Hold on, big brother.

451
00:18:51,304 --> 00:18:52,524
Let me help you set the table.

452
00:18:52,724 --> 00:18:53,564
Go on, Kobito.

453
00:18:53,564 --> 00:18:55,844
Tell Maria thank you for the birthday present.

454
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:57,364
Thank you.

455
00:18:58,144 --> 00:18:59,784
Thank you.

456
00:19:00,364 --> 00:19:01,024
Ah, poop.

457
00:19:01,304 --> 00:19:01,564
What?

458
00:19:01,904 --> 00:19:03,384
Did you just say something to me?

459
00:19:04,144 --> 00:19:05,464
Never mind, dumb bun.

460
00:19:05,484 --> 00:19:06,524
What was that for, pooper?

461
00:19:06,544 --> 00:19:07,104
Juck race?

462
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:07,784
Dabby-dabby-toilet-head?

463
00:19:07,904 --> 00:19:08,784
Give me back that breast.

464
00:19:08,904 --> 00:19:09,944
Meal and rip it.

465
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:10,744
You're pooping it.

466
00:19:12,704 --> 00:19:14,164
Thanks for the awesome meal.

467
00:19:14,604 --> 00:19:16,144
I barely got any beef.

468
00:19:16,364 --> 00:19:18,164
There were at least four pounds worth, too.

469
00:19:19,464 --> 00:19:21,204
Those girls have quite the appetite.

470
00:19:21,444 --> 00:19:22,404
Hey, so do you.

471
00:19:23,824 --> 00:19:25,804
All that food is making me tired.

472
00:19:26,604 --> 00:19:28,964
Hey, Kodika, do you mind if we stay the night?

473
00:19:29,204 --> 00:19:30,284
It's okay by me.

474
00:19:30,944 --> 00:19:31,384
Seriously?

475
00:19:32,484 --> 00:19:33,204
Thanks, bro.

476
00:19:33,204 --> 00:19:36,684
There is no way you're only 15.

477
00:19:37,044 --> 00:19:38,884
Fine, I turned 16 a while back.

478
00:19:39,124 --> 00:19:40,084
Here, check this out.

479
00:19:40,424 --> 00:19:42,024
Maria gave it to me on my birthday.

480
00:19:42,584 --> 00:19:44,264
Hey, that's a nice locket.

481
00:19:45,084 --> 00:19:46,164
What's with the bug?

482
00:19:46,424 --> 00:19:47,984
Maria gave me the cicada shell,

483
00:19:48,084 --> 00:19:50,764
and I got a buddy to make it into a totally wicked necklace.

484
00:19:51,644 --> 00:19:53,804
It's the only thing that girl has ever given me.

485
00:19:57,724 --> 00:19:59,664
Your life has been kind of rough, huh?

486
00:19:59,864 --> 00:20:01,004
Hey, I'm a big sister.

487
00:20:01,164 --> 00:20:02,064
It is what it is.

488
00:20:03,044 --> 00:20:05,244
Maria, big brother's letting us stay for the night.

489
00:20:07,444 --> 00:20:08,464
Come on, get up.

490
00:20:08,504 --> 00:20:09,144
You need a bath.

491
00:20:09,224 --> 00:20:10,584
I want one with big brother.

492
00:20:11,164 --> 00:20:12,124
Hurry it up, girl!

493
00:20:12,124 --> 00:20:14,224
I'm excited to be nice and washing to you.

494
00:20:14,284 --> 00:20:14,944
You better be great!

495
00:20:15,284 --> 00:20:17,844
I'll check and see if we have any pajamas that'll fit you.

496
00:20:17,844 --> 00:20:20,444
Let me go!

497
00:20:20,444 --> 00:20:20,464
Let me go!

498
00:20:20,464 --> 00:20:21,304
Help you open up!

499
00:20:21,304 --> 00:20:22,764
Shut up and hold still!

500
00:20:23,804 --> 00:20:26,524
I'm glad Cobito isn't that hard to deal with.

501
00:20:26,524 --> 00:20:26,824
Hey!

502
00:20:33,824 --> 00:20:34,644
Cobito?

503
00:20:34,644 --> 00:20:42,764
You gonna take a picture?

504
00:20:43,164 --> 00:20:44,144
No, I'm sorry!

505
00:20:44,244 --> 00:20:44,864
I'm so sorry!

506
00:20:48,904 --> 00:20:51,264
No wonder you wanted us to stay the night.

507
00:20:51,264 --> 00:20:52,264
I'm sorry about that, Kate.

508
00:20:52,264 --> 00:20:53,264
Fine.

509
00:20:53,264 --> 00:20:54,264
I forgive you.

510
00:20:54,264 --> 00:20:55,264
Huh?

511
00:20:55,264 --> 00:20:56,264
Well, that was quick.

512
00:20:56,264 --> 00:20:59,444
Well, I'm pretty sure you didn't stumble in on purpose.

513
00:20:59,444 --> 00:21:00,644
Of course I didn't!

514
00:21:00,644 --> 00:21:01,144
Jeez!

515
00:21:01,144 --> 00:21:01,644
Exactly!

516
00:21:01,644 --> 00:21:04,644
So it's not worth getting all pissed off at you.

517
00:21:04,644 --> 00:21:08,244
It's cool that you're not making up excuses or trying to defend yourself.

518
00:21:08,244 --> 00:21:11,864
Yeah, when I do something bad, I think it's best to own up to it.

519
00:21:11,864 --> 00:21:13,864
You really are a halfway decent guy.

520
00:21:13,864 --> 00:21:17,004
It totally makes sense why Pegasus likes you as much as he does.

521
00:21:17,004 --> 00:21:19,344
Oh, do you and the president know each other?

522
00:21:19,344 --> 00:21:19,844
Sure.

523
00:21:19,844 --> 00:21:22,044
Me and Pegasus are actually fishing buddies.

524
00:21:22,044 --> 00:21:24,544
We go out IU fishing once or twice a month.

525
00:21:24,544 --> 00:21:27,044
Uh, that's super random.

526
00:21:27,044 --> 00:21:28,424
It's fun.

527
00:21:28,424 --> 00:21:29,924
You ought to come along sometime.

528
00:21:29,924 --> 00:21:30,844
Yeah?

529
00:21:30,844 --> 00:21:31,844
Maybe someday.

530
00:21:31,844 --> 00:21:39,644
Hey, thanks for letting us crash.

531
00:21:39,644 --> 00:21:40,644
Till next time.

532
00:21:40,644 --> 00:21:41,644
Yeah.

533
00:21:41,644 --> 00:21:42,644
See you guys at school.

534
00:21:42,644 --> 00:21:43,644
Ah.

535
00:21:43,644 --> 00:21:44,644
Man.

536
00:21:44,644 --> 00:21:47,644
Sometimes I wish that you really were our bigger brother.

537
00:21:47,644 --> 00:21:49,644
Then again.

538
00:21:49,644 --> 00:21:53,644
To be honest, I wouldn't mind if you were more than just a brother, because that way,

539
00:21:53,644 --> 00:21:55,644
you could walk in on me all the time.

540
00:21:55,644 --> 00:21:58,644
But you do have Senna, so, well, that's out.

541
00:21:58,644 --> 00:21:59,644
Alrighty.

542
00:21:59,644 --> 00:22:00,644
See ya.

543
00:22:01,844 --> 00:22:07,844
It wasn't long before I figured out what Kate was getting at.

544
00:22:07,844 --> 00:22:09,844
It wasn't very long at all.

545
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:45,253
That was delicious! Let's go home and take a nap.

546
00:23:45,253 --> 00:23:47,253
Hey! Do the preview like a normal person, Hag!

547
00:23:47,253 --> 00:23:49,253
Yeah, whatever, you annoying brat.

548
00:23:49,253 --> 00:23:51,253
Next, my childhood friend is too much of a battleground.

549
00:23:51,253 --> 00:23:55,253
If Big Brother has childhood friends, that means he's all grown up!

550
00:23:55,253 --> 00:23:57,253
I want to have a childhood friend, too!

551
00:23:57,253 --> 00:23:59,253
Don't be dense, you're still in your childhood.

552
00:23:59,253 --> 00:24:03,253
Though in another five years, I bet Kobotel could be your childhood friend.

553
00:24:03,253 --> 00:24:06,253
I don't want no poopy vampire to be my childhood friend!

554
00:24:06,253 --> 00:24:09,253
You and her will be my enemies forever! Take that, poopy Hag!

555
00:24:09,253 --> 00:24:10,253
Fine, fine.

556
00:24:11,253 --> 00:24:13,253
Thank you, Jenga.

557
00:24:13,253 --> 00:24:15,253
Um, it's possible to not understand my heart, just like you said,

558
00:24:15,253 --> 00:24:29,253
I'm so hungry!

559
00:24:29,253 --> 00:24:30,253
Oh no!

560
00:24:31,293 --> 00:24:36,253
I would like that to be so cold!

